PROPOSED LOGIC

1. Identify the returned claim using the F8 reference.

select
@claim_id = c.claim_id
, @claim_workflow_id = c.claim_workflow_id
from dbo.x12_837_2300_REF ref
inner join mcr_dc_prod.dbo.claim c
on c.claim_id = convert(int, ref.L2300_ref02_reference)
where ref.x12_837_2300_id = @x12_837_2300_id
and ref.L2300_ref01_code = ‘F8’
and isnumeric(ref.L2300_ref02_reference) = 1

2. Get workflow types from repricing configuration.

select top 1
@inprocess_claim_workflow_type_id = rc.in_process_claim_workflow_type_id
, @review_claim_workflow_type_id = rc.review_claim_workflow_type_id
from dbo.repricing_configuration rc with (nolock)
where rc.inbound_trading_partner_file_type_id = @trading_partner_file_type_id
and rc.deleted = 0

3. Translate In Process workflow type to actual workflow id.

select top 1
@inprocess_claim_workflow_id = cw.claim_workflow_id
from mcr_dc_prod.dbo.claim_workflow cw with (nolock)
where cw.claim_workflow_type_id = @inprocess_claim_workflow_type_id
order by cw.sequence_number

4. Translate Review workflow type to actual workflow id.

select top 1
@review_claim_workflow_id = cw.claim_workflow_id
from mcr_dc_prod.dbo.claim_workflow cw with (nolock)
where cw.claim_workflow_type_id = @review_claim_workflow_type_id
order by cw.sequence_number

5. Only move the claim if it is currently sitting in the configured In Process workflow.

if @claim_id is not null
and @claim_workflow_id = @inprocess_claim_workflow_id
and @review_claim_workflow_id is not null
begin

set @claim_comment =
    'This claim was returned on '
    + isnull(@trading_partner_filename,'')
    + ' but could not be imported due to '
    + isnull(@error_reason,'file errors')
update mcr_dc_prod.dbo.claim
set claim_workflow_id = @review_claim_workflow_id
  , date_modified = getdate()
  , os_user_name = suser_sname()
where claim_id = @claim_id
insert into mcr_dc_prod.dbo.claim_comment
(
      claim_id
    , comment
    , active
    , created_date
    , created_user_id
    , modified_date
    , modified_user_id
    , deleted
    , claim_comment_type_id
)
values
(
      @claim_id
    , @claim_comment
    , 1
    , getdate()
    , 0
    , getdate()
    , 0
    , 0
    , null
)

end

6. Continue existing processing exactly as today.

update dbo.x12_837_2300
set error = 1,
processed = 1
where x12_837_2300_id = @x12_837_2300_id

goto NEXT_CLAIM

IMPLEMENTATION FLOW

1. Returned claim identified from F8 reference.
2. In Process workflow type pulled from repricing_configuration.
3. Review workflow type pulled from repricing_configuration.
4. Workflow types translated to actual claim_workflow_id values using claim_workflow.
5. Verify claim is currently in the configured In Process workflow.
6. Update claim.claim_workflow_id to Review workflow.
7. Insert comment into claim_comment.
8. Continue existing x12_837_2300 error/processed logic unchanged.
9. Continue processing via NEXT_CLAIM.

